      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T15:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are we a USB device?  From what I\u0027ve heard, there\u0027s some limited device support required for some kind of factory or TBT cert testing involving the DUT being a UFP.  But otherwise, we don\u0027t generally have support as a USB device.",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39c02abd_22813558",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329118
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T00:55:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The history was EC set 1 to VDO[bit26], but we set Modal_Operation_Supported_SOP\u003d0 in VIF.\n\nAnd according to VIF(Vendor Info File Specification: version 3.20), This field shall be set to the value of Type_C_Is_Alt_Mode_Adapter.\n\nIn VIF spec, If Type_C_Can_Act_As_Device is not set to YES, then this field shall be set to NO.\n\nAfter Type_C_Can_Act_As_Device be set to 1, the Data_Capable_as_USB_Device_SOP will auto-set to 1.\n\nIf Data_Capable_as_USB_Device_SOP is 1, the tester will check if EC return VDO[bit30]\u003d1 which match to VIF.",
      "parentUuid": "720b9ba2_272c55ac",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66eb08c4_feb6d7fa",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T18:15:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Scott: I follow the VIF logic, but I can\u0027t remember what prompted you to set `Type_C_Can_Act_As_Device` to true in the first place. Can you remind me?",
      "parentUuid": "39c02abd_22813558",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85387923_540b7d13",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329118
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T09:00:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We want Modal_Operation_Supported_SOP \u003d 1, so we need to set Type_C_Is_Alt_Mode_Adapter \u003d 1. But Type_C_Is_Alt_Mode_Adapter is gray-out and cannot be modified. And in VIF spec, `Type_C_Is_Alt_Mode_Adapter (Y/N)` section, it said \n```\nIf Type_C_Can_Act_As_Device is not set to YES, then this field shall be set to NO.\n```\nSo I set Type_C_Can_Act_As_Device \u003d 1, the Type_C_Is_Alt_Mode_Adapter can be modified and Modal_Operation_Supported_SOP will be 1 automatically.",
      "parentUuid": "66eb08c4_feb6d7fa",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7d2dea2_34450dd0",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T23:17:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Diana: I see everything Scott just pointed out, but it doesn\u0027t make sense to me that you _must_ be a USB device to be an alt mode adapter. Is that true?\n\nI have a vague memory of having this conversation before, and it was something like, you need to support a Billboard device just so you can tell the other side that you can\u0027t do anything else.\n\nScott: I\u0027ll note that supporting TBT as a UFP is an off-by-default testing feature here, so I\u0027m fairly OK with just giving the tester what it wants. However, unless something changed in the past year or so, our AP software is not actually going to act like a USB device as UFP.",
      "parentUuid": "85387923_540b7d13",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30f6e2d8_9153eea1",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T17:09:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It makes general sense to me that if you support entering an alternate mode as a UFP, you should also be a USB device.  We\u0027re in a very non-standard position with what we are capable of.  I sometimes wonder if more of this should only be advertised at runtime when unlocked with a host command to avoid exposing this state on compliance and customer systems.\n\nIt\u0027s alright to code this to be consistent for compliance.  Hopefully other port partners in the ecosystem don\u0027t take this bit too seriously.",
      "parentUuid": "c7d2dea2_34450dd0",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65dcd78a_cc9a043f",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T15:14:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t we expect the muxes to be in TBT mode before mode exit? \n\nI assume we want to NAK if we hadn\u0027t actually been in TBT mode before the ExitMode came, and ACK if we were in TBT mode.  Though obviously if the compliance tests say otherwise, we can also ACK when we weren\u0027t previously in the mode.",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e575a54_fd5896b3",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1329118
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T00:55:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My original thought was follow SPEC said that we should in USB operation or the USB Safe State. But I think check mux to be in TBT mode before exit will make more sense because we will enter TBT mode before exit it.\n\nShould we just check `USB_PD_MUX_TBT_COMPAT_ENABLED` or also check `USB_PD_MUX_USB_ENABLED` and `USB_PD_MUX_SAFE_MODE`?",
      "parentUuid": "65dcd78a_cc9a043f",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e139cff_1b396822",
        "filename": "baseboard/brya/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 248,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T18:15:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From PD rev 1.3, v 1.4, ss 6.4.4.3.5 Exit Mode Command (I know v 1.5 was published):\n\u003e The Responder Shall ... only return a NAK acknowledgement to a request not containing an Active Mode (i.e., Invalid object position).\n\nI take that to mean that the TCPM should NAK an Exit Mode if we haven\u0027t previously entered a mode. (The language seems to allow for an ACK, but it would be a no-op.) The canonical way to check active modes in our codebase is `pd_get_partner_active_modes`. If the returned structure doesn\u0027t contain the SVID from the _Exit Mode_`, the TCPM should NAK.",
      "parentUuid": "2e575a54_fd5896b3",
      "revId": "7927e70d3a0142dda6f529a7ba8346322f92fe27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
